The European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) is a pivotal entity in this community, responsible for evaluating scientific evidence related to food safety and nutrition within the EU. EFSA provides independent scientific advice on food-related risks, including the assessment of food additives and the establishment of acceptable daily intake levels. Its comprehensive evaluations and guidance are essential for safeguarding food safety and promoting informed decision-making regarding nutrition in the EU. EFSA's collaboration with the World Health Organization further enhances its influence on food safety standards [Data: Entities (7892); Relationships (16453, 16793)].

