This community centers around the complex interplay between Trastornos de la Conducta Alimentaria (TCA) and diabetes management, particularly in patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (DM1). Key entities include patients struggling with TCA, their family histories, and the medical support systems involved in their care.

## TCA's impact on diabetes management

Trastornos de la Conducta Alimentaria (TCA) significantly complicates the management of diabetes, particularly for patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (DM1). The relationship between TCA and diabetes is critical, as patients may exhibit restrictive eating and purging behaviors that can lead to poor metabolic control. This necessitates comprehensive care strategies that address both the psychological and physical health needs of the patient. The severity of TCA may even require involuntary treatment to ensure patient safety, highlighting the urgent need for effective intervention strategies. [Data: Entities (6794, 6790); Relationships (3254, 13085)]

