## Role of multidisciplinary care

A multidisciplinary team is essential in addressing the challenges posed by TCA in patients with diabetes. This team typically includes endocrinologists, nutritionists, and mental health professionals who collaborate to create a comprehensive care plan. Such an approach is vital for managing the complex needs of patients, ensuring that both their physical and psychological health are prioritized. The effectiveness of this team-based care model can significantly influence patient outcomes and quality of life. [Data: Entities (6794, 6791); Relationships (5500)]

