## Psychological factors influencing eating disorders

Eating disorders are significantly influenced by psychological factors, including body image issues and societal pressures. Groups such as models and athletes are at higher risk for developing these disorders due to the pressures to maintain specific body types. Understanding these psychological influences is essential for developing effective prevention and treatment strategies for eating disorders. [Data: Entities (8880, 8882, 8881, 8886, +more); Relationships (8708, 8709, 8712, +more)]

