Hormone replacement therapy (HRT) is often considered for managing symptoms in postmenopausal women, but it carries associated risks, particularly concerning breast cancer. The relationship between HRT and cancer risk is critical for understanding the health implications for individuals with Klinefelter Syndrome, as they may also be affected by hormonal imbalances. This highlights the need for careful consideration of HRT in both male and female populations [Data: Entities (5547); Relationships (11716, 1450)].# Nutritional Health and Essential Fatty Acids Community

