Homocysteine is an amino acid that, when elevated, is associated with an increased risk of developing Alzheimer's disease and other forms of cognitive decline. High levels of homocysteine can damage blood vessels and are linked to cardiovascular diseases, further complicating cognitive health. Monitoring and managing homocysteine levels through dietary interventions, such as increasing Vitamin B intake, is crucial for preventing associated health risks. This relationship emphasizes the need for awareness and proactive management of homocysteine levels in at-risk populations. [Data: Entities (3208, 3216, 3219); Relationships (5615, 8501, 8523, 11355, 11352)]

