## Glycogen storage disease and its implications

Glycogen storage disease refers to a group of inherited metabolic disorders that can have severe health consequences. These disorders arise from enzyme deficiencies that disrupt normal glycogen metabolism, leading to its accumulation in various tissues. The complexity of these diseases necessitates ongoing research and clinical management, making the associated entities crucial for advancing knowledge and treatment options [Data: Entities (9517); Relationships (16577, 17760)].

