PLOS ONE is a multidisciplinary journal that publishes a wide range of research, including studies on nutrition and cancer. Its commitment to open access allows for broad dissemination of important findings, making it a vital platform for researchers in the field. Notably, PLOS ONE has published significant studies related to swallowing disorders in cancer patients, highlighting its relevance to the community's focus on nutritional outcomes [Data: Entities (223); Relationships (2126, 2193)].

## BMC Cancer's focus on nutritional outcomes

BMC Cancer is dedicated to publishing research related to cancer, including studies on nutritional outcomes for patients. The journal has featured the PROPILS trial, which investigates preoperative immunonutrition in liver resection for cancer, showcasing its commitment to advancing knowledge in this critical area. BMC Cancer serves as a key resource for researchers and clinicians looking to understand the impact of nutrition on cancer treatment and patient quality of life [Data: Entities (7687); Relationships (16547, 14096)].

## The significance of the PROPILS trial

The PROPILS trial is a multicenter randomized controlled trial studying the effects of preoperative immunonutrition in patients undergoing liver resection for cancer. This trial is significant as it aims to provide evidence on how nutritional interventions can improve surgical outcomes and overall patient care. The trial's findings are expected to influence clinical practices and guidelines regarding nutritional support in oncology [Data: Entities (14999); Relationships (16547)].

