The Critical Care specialty emphasizes the importance of managing hyperglycemia in critically ill patients, particularly those receiving nutritional support. Publications in this field provide valuable insights into the implications of hyperglycemia and its management, contributing to the development of effective treatment protocols. The intersection of critical care and nutritional management is essential for improving patient outcomes, as hyperglycemia can significantly impact recovery and overall health [Data: Entities (12878); Relationships (1060, 9782)].

