Preterm newborns have unique nutritional needs that differ significantly from those of term newborns. Their increased risk of malnutrition necessitates specialized dietary plans and formulas to support their growth and development. The nutritional guidelines specifically address these needs, ensuring that preterm infants receive adequate nutrition to prevent complications such as necrotizing enterocolitis and other health issues. [Data: Entities (2609, 2614); Relationships (10341, 10344, 10345, 2098, +more)]

