Morley JE is a leading researcher in the field of frailty and aging, known for his extensive contributions, including significant studies on sarcopenia and limited mobility in older adults. His work has been instrumental in shaping the understanding of frailty as a key component of aging, advocating for improved care strategies for the elderly population. Morley JE's involvement in the development of the frailty consensus highlights his influence in establishing standardized approaches to managing frailty, which is crucial for enhancing elderly care practices. [Data: Entities (3092); Relationships (1682, 11075, 11073, 11074)]

