Frailty syndrome is a major health concern for the elderly, characterized by decreased functionality and increased vulnerability to adverse health events. It is associated with higher risks of hospitalization and mortality, making it essential to address this condition through targeted interventions. The frailty syndrome is treatable and reversible, which underscores the importance of early intervention and comprehensive care strategies to improve outcomes for older adults [Data: Entities (3101); Relationships (2068, 9006)].

