Exercise is recognized as a crucial intervention for older adults, significantly enhancing their physical and cognitive health. Regular physical activity is essential for managing various health conditions, including diabetes, hypertension, and frailty. It also plays a vital role in preventing sarcopenia, a condition characterized by muscle loss, which is particularly prevalent in the elderly. Engaging in regular exercise can improve muscle mass and function, thereby promoting independence and a better quality of life for older adults. [Data: Entities (3179, 3180); Relationships (5787, 1747, 11020, 10967, 10860, +more)]

