Ascites, the accumulation of fluid in the abdominal cavity, is a common complication of cirrhosis that can complicate nutritional assessments and dietary management. Patients with ascites often require specific dietary restrictions to manage their condition effectively. The relationship between ascites and cirrhosis highlights the need for comprehensive care strategies that address both nutritional and medical needs. [Data: Entities (608, 10144); Relationships (4380, 4376)]

