Fatty acids are crucial components of dietary lipids, significantly impacting nutrition and health, especially concerning cardiovascular diseases. They serve as building blocks for lipids and are vital for energy storage and cellular function. Fatty acids like ALA, EPA, and DHA are recognized for their positive effects on heart health, making them essential in various nutritional formulas. Their importance is underscored by their role in the absorption of water and electrolytes, as well as energy support for the lungs, including the synthesis of pulmonary surfactant. [Data: Entities (2156); Relationships (9026, 3855, 9018)]

