The autonomous communities in Spain have their own regulations regarding healthcare and patient rights, leading to variations in the management of dysphagia and related dietary provisions. This decentralized approach can result in inconsistencies in the availability and quality of care across different regions. The SNS collaborates with these communities to ensure that health services are effectively managed, but the differences in regulations can complicate the implementation of standardized care for dysphagia patients. Understanding these regional differences is crucial for improving healthcare delivery [Data: Entities (15802); Relationships (14337, 1882)].# Home Artificial Nutrition Community

The community focuses on home artificial nutrition, encompassing various entities involved in providing nutritional support to patients unable to consume adequate nutrition orally. Key entities include NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA, GRUPO NADYA-SENPE, and NUTRICI√ìN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA, which are interconnected through their roles in delivering and managing nutritional therapies at home.

## NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA as a vital intervention

NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA (NPD) is essential for patients with intestinal failure, allowing them to receive necessary nutrients intravenously at home. This method significantly enhances the quality of life for patients who cannot obtain nutrition through oral means, reducing hospital visits and associated complications. The practice is documented by the NADYA group, which tracks its health implications and costs, emphasizing its importance in patient care [Data: Entities (2061); Relationships (3478, 4629, 4976)].

