The community is centered around NADYA and NADYA-SENPE, which focus on home enteral and parenteral nutrition in Spain. Key entities include researchers and organizations that contribute to the understanding and management of nutritional care, particularly for patients with neurological diseases and other health conditions. Their collaborative efforts enhance the quality of life for patients requiring specialized nutritional support.

## NADYA's pivotal role in nutritional support

NADYA is a comprehensive group dedicated to the study and support of artificial nutrition, particularly in home and outpatient settings in Spain. Established in 1992, it has maintained a registry that collects and reports data on patients receiving home parenteral nutrition (NPD) and complications related to enteral nutrition. This extensive data collection is crucial for understanding the needs of patients requiring specialized nutritional care, especially those suffering from neurological diseases. The group's focus on enhancing nutritional support aims to improve patient outcomes significantly [Data: Entities (12188); Relationships (4128, 878, 5623)].

