NADYA-SENPE operates as a specialized working group in Spain, maintaining various national registries related to home enteral nutrition. This includes annual registries of enteral and parenteral nutrition, which have been conducted since the late 1990s. Their involvement in research concerning health-related quality of life for patients receiving home nutritional support is vital for advancing the understanding and management of nutritional care in Spain. The group's data collection efforts since 1992 have established a robust foundation for ongoing research and policy development in nutritional support [Data: Entities (16297); Relationships (4132, 246)].

