Vitamin E is recognized for its antioxidant properties, which help protect cells from oxidative stress. It is particularly relevant in managing conditions like Alzheimer's disease and coronary disease, where oxidative damage is a concern. Studies indicate that Vitamin E can inhibit lipid peroxidation, thereby safeguarding cell membranes from damage, highlighting its importance in nutritional therapies [Data: Reports (607); Entities (3440, 3447); Relationships (4715, 8438, 5617)].

