Vitamin C is essential for tissue repair and immune function, enhancing iron absorption and playing a role in reducing oxidative stress in various health conditions, including cancer. However, excessive intake can lead to complications, emphasizing the need for careful management in clinical settings. Its inclusion in parenteral nutrition formulations is crucial for preventing deficiencies [Data: Reports (607); Entities (2005, 3440); Relationships (2719, 8512, 8516)].

