The relationships between vitamins E and C and chronic diseases such as diabetes and obesity underscore the importance of these nutrients in managing long-term health conditions. For example, Vitamin E's role in reducing oxidative stress can be beneficial for patients with diabetes, while Vitamin C's effects on iron absorption are crucial for those with dietary restrictions [Data: Reports (607); Entities (3447, 2005); Relationships (1905, 5814)].

