Dietary adaptations are crucial for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia to ensure safe swallowing and adequate nutrition. The development of modified texture diets, such as traditional and commercial options, is essential for meeting the specific needs of these patients. These dietary modifications help prevent complications like aspiration pneumonia and malnutrition, which are common among individuals with swallowing difficulties. The relationship between dysphagia and nutritional support is significant, as proper dietary management can greatly enhance patient quality of life [Data: Reports (906); Entities (929, 928, 675); Relationships (170, 175, 211, 107, 106, +more)].

