Cancer patients often face significant challenges in maintaining nutritional intake due to the effects of their condition and treatment. Artificial nutrition plays a crucial role in managing these patients, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery. The relationship between cancer treatment and nutritional support underscores the importance of integrated care strategies in oncology. [Data: Reports (1110); Entities (1635); Relationships (6760, 6806)]

