Eating disorders, such as anorexia nervosa, significantly affect the nutritional status of individuals within the PACIENTES community. These patients often require specialized nutritional support and psychotherapy to address both their psychological and dietary needs. The interplay between mental health and nutrition is crucial, as effective treatment for eating disorders must incorporate comprehensive dietary education and support [Data: Reports (2115); Entities (8928, 8892); Relationships (3467, 517)].

