V√≥mitos incoercibles represent a severe medical condition characterized by uncontrollable vomiting, which can lead to dehydration and nutritional deficiencies. This condition complicates the administration of enteral nutrition, making it essential to explore alternative nutritional support methods, such as parenteral nutrition. The management of v√≥mitos incoercibles is crucial for preventing further health complications and ensuring adequate dietary support for affected individuals [Data: Reports (1214); Entities (4859); Relationships (4823, 2833, 3721)].

## The role of nutritional support in patient recovery

