Entities like the Endocrine Society and UpToDate collaborate to provide clinical practice guidelines that reference 'Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.' This integration ensures that recommendations for managing endocrine disorders are informed by established medical literature, enhancing clinical practice and patient care. The collaboration underscores the importance of comprehensive resources in endocrinology [Data: Reports (1283); Entities (5127, 5117); Relationships (14580, 14584, 14589)].

