The Williams Textbook of Endocrinology is co-authored by several leading endocrinologists, including Melmed S, Kronenberg HM, Polonsky KS, and Larsen PR. This collaboration ensures a comprehensive exploration of endocrine disorders, making it an essential reference for medical professionals. The collective expertise of these authors enhances the textbook's authority and relevance in clinical settings, covering topics from hormonal regulation to specific disorders like insulinoma and pheochromocytoma [Data: Entities (5056, 3703, 3705, 3702); Relationships (12271, 12272, 12280)].

