## Ministerio de Sanidad y Consumo as the regulatory body

The Ministerio de Sanidad y Consumo is the primary governmental body responsible for regulating public health in Spain. It oversees the creation of health policies, including those related to eating disorders, and is involved in the implementation of laws such as Ley 41/2002. This central role positions the ministry as a key player in shaping health guidelines and practices across the country, impacting both healthcare providers and patients. The ministry's relationships with various organizations, such as the Grupo de Trabajo de la Gu√≠a de Pr√°ctica Cl√≠nica, further emphasize its influence in the development of clinical guidelines for managing eating disorders [Data: Entities (4953); Relationships (14377, 14375)].

