ESPEN develops tailored guidelines for various patient populations, including those with specific conditions such as cancer, liver disease, and diabetes. These guidelines provide healthcare professionals with evidence-based recommendations for nutritional interventions that address the unique needs of these patients. For instance, ESPEN's guidelines for cancer patients emphasize the importance of nutritional support in improving treatment outcomes and quality of life. By focusing on the specific requirements of different patient groups, ESPEN ensures that nutritional care is both effective and relevant [Data: Reports (685); Relationships (2933, 2917, 2922, 2949, 2951, +more)].

