Dysphagia affects approximately 3% of the general population, particularly among individuals with conditions such as strokes and neurodegenerative diseases. This condition can lead to severe complications, including malnutrition and aspiration pneumonia, which significantly impact patients' quality of life. The need for specialized dietary modifications and interventions underscores the importance of addressing dysphagia in clinical practice. [Data: Reports (2064); Entities (11, 4872, 2886); Relationships (294, 376, 273)]

