## Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 and eating disorders

Individuals with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 are at an increased risk of developing eating disorders, such as Anorexia Nervosa and Bulimia Nervosa, due to the pressures of managing their weight and insulin intake. This relationship highlights the psychological challenges faced by patients and the need for integrated care approaches that address both diabetes management and mental health. [Data: Reports (399); Relationships (8704, 13387, +more)]

