The ATA has developed specific guidelines for the diagnosis and management of thyroid disease during pregnancy and the postpartum period, which are critical for ensuring the health of both mothers and infants. These guidelines address the use of medications like propylthiouracil (PTU) and the management of thyroid conditions that may arise during pregnancy. The involvement of experts such as Brent GA and Alexander EK in these guidelines highlights the importance of tailored recommendations for this vulnerable population. The ATA's focus on pregnancy-related thyroid health reflects its commitment to improving patient outcomes across different life stages. [Data: Reports (421); Entities (4558, 4434, 4578); Relationships (13755, 13756, 13757)]

